{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs","id":1299424,"title":"Forces objects/constructs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-24T15:23:39-07:00","id":1299424,"title":"Forces objects/constructs","content":"The Forces sphere is capable of creating illusions that covers all human senses, including touch. Then, a mage can create an object (or transmute Forces, let's consider Prime 2 will be added for argument's sake) ou of nowhere using Forces. I wonder how much successes would be necessary for that and how strong would be the object?<br /> <br /> What if the mage wants to create a force cage around an enemy, or a set of rope/chains to contain someone. How much successes are required and would they be indestructible? Probably not, should we work with the Objects durability/structure of M20? How does that works with the Arete roll?<br /> <br /> Also, I ask for intersting Forces effects like that, that aren't covered in any book. Forces is a very useful sphere and it's my favorite, so bring some nice ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T22:29:59-07:00","id":1299521,"title":"","content":"Note that for conjuring forces with Prime 2, you need Forces 3.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure if you're not mixing up some stuff. For literally illusionary things you need Mind, not Forces - that is, making somebody imagine things that aren't there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You *can* of course use Forces to simulate things for a person - make somebody see stuff that isn't there (light), get touched/stopped by kinetic forces or hear things that aren't there, but forces don't cover the illusionary part of smell and taste.<br /> <br /> But I guess that's just nitpicking on the term 'illusion' at this time. Anyways, to make an actual cage or ropes they can't escape? Yeah, I think you seriously need Forces 3/Prime 2, because pulling the forces necessary to withstand a strong character's struggle...you need a lot of surrounding force to do that, and IMO neither a noisy street, nor a set of lightbulbs in the area provides enough forces to divert into anything like strong restraints - unless you, again, have higher Forces to do that with a large area.<br /> <br /> Now, presuming Prime 2/Forces 3, I'd use the damage table for the 'strength' result in a Grappling challenge - essentially the Damage result as the 'Strength' roll of the restraints 'grappling' the target. It seems like a reasonable scaling to me for that situation if you want to make a sort of forces 'rope'.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> The only problem I see is that per the rules and depending on ST, you need either a constant supply of Quintessence to keep up the forces for something like an invisible 'cage' ( Which is why Force Field Generators exist in case of technomancers! ), or probably constant concentration of the caster to keep up the invisible restraints on a specific individual or individuals - that is, make the force target based instead of space-based - unless you 'lock on' the invisible ropes to their pattern, which mixes a higher level of Life (~3) into the required spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-25-2019, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:13:17-07:00","id":1299586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs?p=1299521#post1299521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that for conjuring forces with Prime 2, you need Forces 3.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure if you're not mixing up some stuff. For literally illusionary things you need Mind, not Forces - that is, making somebody imagine things that aren't there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You *can* of course use Forces to simulate things for a person - make somebody see stuff that isn't there (light), get touched/stopped by kinetic forces or hear things that aren't there, but forces don't cover the illusionary part of smell and taste.<br /> <br /> But I guess that's just nitpicking on the term 'illusion' at this time. Anyways, to make an actual cage or ropes they can't escape? Yeah, I think you seriously need Forces 3/Prime 2, because pulling the forces necessary to withstand a strong character's struggle...you need a lot of surrounding force to do that, and IMO neither a noisy street, nor a set of lightbulbs in the area provides enough forces to divert into anything like strong restraints - unless you, again, have higher Forces to do that with a large area.<br /> <br /> Now, presuming Prime 2/Forces 3, I'd use the damage table for the 'strength' result in a Grappling challenge - essentially the Damage result as the 'Strength' roll of the restraints 'grappling' the target. It seems like a reasonable scaling to me for that situation if you want to make a sort of forces 'rope'.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> The only problem I see is that per the rules and depending on ST, you need either a constant supply of Quintessence to keep up the forces for something like an invisible 'cage' ( Which is why Force Field Generators exist in case of technomancers! ), or probably constant concentration of the caster to keep up the invisible restraints on a specific individual or individuals - that is, make the force target based instead of space-based - unless you 'lock on' the invisible ropes to their pattern, which mixes a higher level of Life (~3) into the required spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be surprised by the ammount of forces that surround us. But that's another matter.<br /> <br /> You mean that the target would have to achieve as much successes in the strength roll as the &quot;damage&quot; rolled by the mage's Arete to break free? Looks like a good call.<br /> <br /> And what about breaking objects? What if it's a cage? Or if the mage created a chair and someone wants to break it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:55:44-07:00","id":1299598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs?p=1299586#post1299586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd be surprised by the ammount of forces that surround us. But that's another matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is if it's beneficial to the structural integrity of the surroundings, if enough forces to seriously hold a person get taken away from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about breaking objects? What if it's a cage? Or if the mage created a chair and someone wants to break it? </div> </div> </div>I don't actually see constructs of kinetic forces being 'breakable' per se. After all, they are not physical. I presume you can force their way through them like a sort of rubber band, forcing (heh) them aside with enough of your own force, before they snap back into place behind you.<br /> Although wether they do that or 'break', I guess, depends on the paradigm of the caster.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:57:02-07:00","id":1299599,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like durability/structure rules and think that would be a good ocassion to use it. Arete successes could provide 2 dots each to divide between both in any way you want (structure needs to be at least one). This would allow to create fields that are very solid but break instantly if you overpower them, while others can be more &quot;plastic&quot; in their composition to withstand more.<br /> <br /> While Forces has the disadvantage of needing a constant energy supply to keep the field in place, I would argue that they should be able to auto-repair durability damage as long as they keep receiving energy. It's a flux of energy after all, pushing trough it wouldn't necessarily &quot;break&quot; it (although it might &quot;overload&quot; the Instrument, I guess, I would leave that as a matter of Focus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T09:53:20-07:00","id":1299633,"title":"","content":"This does sound like an attempt to get out of having the Matter Sphere. Your mage might see it as coalescing forces, but if you want to create &quot;a physical illusion of a rope that holds someone for a few hours&quot; then you're going to need to invest in Matter. Someone with Spirit could say &quot;Oh I'm going to give him bad dreams, but through his soul, not his mind, so I can use Spirit instead of Mind&quot;; sure, your mage might see it that way, but to give someone bad dreams you need Mind. If you see Mind as an extension of Spirit then feel free to invest EXP so that your Mind and Spirit rating are always equal.<br /> <br /> Forces can create a force that holds you in place, a visual shape that looks like a rope, and can give it the feel of a rope (that's a matter of friction, heat, sensation). But this would be an INCREDIBLY demanding effect in terms of successes, demanding successes for duration, for the multi-sensory aspect of the illusion, for the actual force of the rope holding your arms bound... whereas conjuring a rope (Correspondence + Matter) or creating a rope (Prime + Matter) would be a much simpler effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:36:34-07:00","id":1299650,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>, very nice thinking more about it, it really shouldn't break, the force should only be overwhelmed, like when you make two magnets with the same pole touch. As soon as the force &quot;uniting&quot; (or breaking) them ia gone, they come back as they were. Unless the mage wants it to stop when this happens, making it effectively &quot;break&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> you got it in the 2nd part of your post. It's nothing more than force and visua/touch sensations. It shouldn't require that much successes. <br /> <br /> About it going on the realm of Matter, we see shperes doing things that other spheres do all the time. Theree is always more than 1 way to do things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:55:10-07:00","id":1299654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs?p=1299650#post1299650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> you got it in the 2nd part of your post. It's nothing more than force and visua/touch sensations. It shouldn't require that much successes.<br /> <br /> About it going on the realm of Matter, we see shperes doing things that other spheres do all the time. Theree is always more than 1 way to do things</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more than one way to do things in Mage, yes. My point is that the idea that it's simple to do this with Forces when it would actually be very complicated is a workaround which is trying to avoid investment.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's nothing more than the force holding their hands together, which is going to be a minimum of 2 successes since it's an effect that's influencing another person, plus at least another success if I want it to last for a scene... then there's the whole issue a complicated immersive physical illusion that responds to their movement, giving off a sense of weight, friction and texture, all while being visible. So it's nothing more than about 5 successes or so.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah you can tie people up with &quot;ropes&quot; of energy with Forces whilst also casting an illusion that makes it look like you've used ropes, and make it last long enough that it's worthwhile, but it's not a simple matter of getting 1 or 2 successes.<br /> <br /> Or we could just argue that teleporting some fire from the sun, or one of the hells in the high umbra, is a simple alternative to conjuring fire with Prime + Forces. Yes, there are multiple ways to do thing in Mage. But they often demand far more successes, they've often more difficult, and they're often impractical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-25-2019, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:35:24-07:00","id":1299766,"title":"","content":"I wuldn't say it needs 5 successes. 5 successes is where mighty feats begins.I don't think that creating the sensation and visual of a rope/cage is dificult, it's not even a living being, barely moves.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not like you don't need Matter anymore, you still can't do a lot of things that Matter can with Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:02:51-07:00","id":1299907,"title":"","content":"Well, Matter wouldn't require energy to keep it after the initial creation, for starters.<br /> <br /> Taking and transmuting energy from the environment risks to cause unwanted colateral effects (imagine arcs of energy jumping from plugs, winds blowing, sounds booming and/or dimming...the energy has to travel from where it comes before or after being transmuted), and Quintessence may grow in trees sometimes, but it's never ubiquitous.<br /> <br /> And about the successes, it would require a ton if the &quot;divide successes&quot; rule it's in place. If it isn't then it's easier, but even then it's more complex than just summoning featureless energy. There are rules for illusions in M20 p.303. Under the most generous interpretation (2 sensations and moving) it would require 3 base successes + whatever it's put into the ropes strength (you would need 4+ successes to do a rope)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-26-2019, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T07:57:02-07:00","id":1299952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs?p=1299907#post1299907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about the successes, it would require a ton if the &quot;divide successes&quot; rule it's in place. If it isn't then it's easier, but even then it's more complex than just summoning featureless energy. There are rules for illusions in M20 p.303. Under the most generous interpretation (2 sensations and moving) it would require 3 base successes + whatever it's put into the ropes strength (you would need 4+ successes to do a rope)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, 100% this. I feel like OP is trying to make it sound like a rather trivial effect. It would be trivial to summon a rope out of nothing, if you've got the Quintessence to put into it. Complex physical illusions that trap people is much more demanding. 5+ successes is where you get into major effects, generally, yes, but things can need 5+ successes and not be that cool.<br /> <br /> Essentially the forces method of making ropes is much more success-intensive than the matter method, which is as it should be really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:05:59-07:00","id":1299955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs?p=1299907#post1299907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Matter wouldn't require energy to keep it after the initial creation, for starters.<br /> <br /> Taking and transmuting energy from the environment risks to cause unwanted colateral effects (imagine arcs of energy jumping from plugs, winds blowing, sounds booming and/or dimming...the energy has to travel from where it comes before or after being transmuted), and Quintessence may grow in trees sometimes, but it's never ubiquitous.<br /> <br /> And about the successes, it would require a ton if the &amp;quot;divide successes&amp;quot; rule it's in place. If it isn't then it's easier, but even then it's more complex than just summoning featureless energy. There are rules for illusions in M20 p.303. Under the most generous interpretation (2 sensations and moving) it would require 3 base successes + whatever it's put into the ropes strength (you would need 4+ successes to do a rope)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. An the case where the mage isn't worried about making it look like a real object? Without the feel.<br /> Let's say the mage wants to create a chair of pure energy for someone o sit? Or an umbrella?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:18:22-07:00","id":1299962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299424-forces-objects-constructs?p=1299955#post1299955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. An the case where the mage isn't worried about making it look like a real object? Without the feel.<br /> Let's say the mage wants to create a chair of pure energy for someone o sit? Or an umbrella?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a lot easier, success wise. I would say that 2+ successes (2 being the minimum to affect the outside world) should be enough, unless you need/want to add some into duration. You're out of Illusion rules, and usually the &quot;form&quot; it's free. A case could be made to require more successes if the form it's more complex, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}